WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:01.740
Please welcome Aurora!

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:24.260
Aurora, you have recorded your first album ...

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.240
And on that album, there are songs that ...

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.220
... you wrote ten years ago.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.220
You were nine years old then.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:32.780
Yes.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:39.500
When you listen to these songs, can you hear a difference in how you wrote when you were nine and how you write now?

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.460
Yes, there's probably a little bit of a difference there.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.440
The strange thing is that I wrote «darker» material when I was younger.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.100
I'm a little more ...

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:57.060
... positive in the way I write now, than I was before.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.380
And I think I just ...

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.300
Or, I think that ...

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:08.200
It's usually the other way around, that you see all the nice things when you're little, and then you grow up and realise how bad everything is ...

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:09.780
... behind the facade, sometimes.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:13.960
But it was the other way around with me. I was quite observant. I enjoyed observing things ...

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:16.240
... and people and the world around me.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.980
And I was very sensitive.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:18.980
When I was little.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:21.400
So things really affected me.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:25.720
Do people feel more as children than as adults?

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:28.320
I think ...

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:33.580
I think you have the same amount of feelings as a child and as an adult.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.340
But maybe you ...

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:38.520
You use the brain more when you grow up ...

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.200
... and follow your heart a little less. But I think that you ...

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.880
Maybe you only listen to your heart when you're a child.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.080
What are your thoughts?

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:47.740
I agree. As a child ...

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:52.900
... you live in such a limited world that everything becomes so intensive.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:56.600
And I think it was most evident at 14-15 years old, maybe ...

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:01.080
... because then you had this rush of hormones that caused you to fall in love ...

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:03.560
But at 19, you're quite in control.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:08.320
And I think at that age, you don't allow yourself to feel as much, I think.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:14.780
When you are a part of, as you now are, a music business ...

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:20.260
And you're in the big league, so to say ...

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.360
... there's a huge circus surrounding you.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.660
Is it hard to remain the person you are?

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.400
Uhm, yes.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:28.980
It is, really.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.880
I think it is most of the time.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:36.580
I'm sort of ... I've always known very well who I am as a person.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.300
And what I stand for. And what I want.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:40.600
But ...

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.560
All of a sudden, I had to find out ...

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:48.600
... what I had to be as an artist. And image, and music, and music videos and ...

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:54.240
And these days I've got a quite big team around me ...

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:58.000
And I'm quite small.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:02:59.460
But I ...

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.300
I try to speak louder and louder ...

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:05.380
... with each day that passes, I think that's important.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:10.080
You quit school.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.380
To do this full-time.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:18.500
Do you miss hanging out with people your own age and just ...

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.240
... be with them.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:23.560
I was ...

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.500
I've never been very good a being a young person.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.560
I was very good a being a child.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:31.220
I think I skipped the youth phase.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:34.480
I'm still part child and part adult.

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:41.180
But it has something to do with ... When you're as sensitive as I was ...

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:46.460
I was very easily affected by other people's energies and moods.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:51.180
And what happens ... When you're with young people ...

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:54.820
... like you said, around the age of 14, everyone ...

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.300
Everyone has ...

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:59.380
Or, most young people, at least, have a little bit of chaos within themselves.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:03.920
And you can feel the small storms that are in everyone.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:07.240
And that's why it's quite nice to be with ...

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:11.220
... people who have let the storm calm down a little.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:15.920
At least that's what I think. So I think I fit well with ...

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:18.000
... older people.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:24.340
One of the really big artists in the world today is Katy Perry.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:27.840
And she is a fan of yours.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:31.060
And a lot happened in your career when she ...

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:34.280
... wrote that on Twitter.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:37.840
You suddenly became a very international person.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.840
You've later met her, right? She asked to meet you?

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:50.040
Yes, she came to one of our concerts last year, in L.A..

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:51.960
She was very nice!

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:55.120
I was very nice to see, she came ...

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.080
... as just ...

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:58.520
Katy.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.480
I don't know her real name, it might just be Katy?

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:02.240
... Perry?

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:02.740
Yes?

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.980
But she was just there as herself.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.860
No ...

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.340
... make-up, and no dress and ...

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:13.500
... no wig or stuff like that. She was just very ...

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.340
It was really nice to see ...

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:18.040
... her so real.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.760
She was very down-to-earth. She greeted everyone in the band.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:24.060
And she was just very kind, really.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:27.500
She seemed very genuinely interested in music.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:31.560
And she is just a person who ...

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:32.700
... loves music.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.940
Did you think that you would want her life?

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:36.100
No.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:40.900
It was very nice meeting her, but it was also a little sad.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:42.760
Because you ...

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:46.820
I could sense that she was ...

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:50.820
... a little stressed about being there.

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:53.960
If anyone found out, everyone in ...

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.320
... L.A. would start screaming.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:05:58.720
You ...

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:01.700
You could sense that worry.

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:05.260
She has lost a freedom that ...

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:08.060
... you should have, as a person.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:11.940
To be able to just walk around, being a person.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:13.400
Without being anything else.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:17.520
Because you instantly become so much more, for everyone else.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.720
That's a very strange and unnatural thing, really.

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:24.420
Aurora, thank you so much for being here!

